{{define "content"}}
<div id="page-project-config-workflow">
{{template "project_config_header" $}}

<div class="section card" id="project-ship">
  <h2>Shipping</h2>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:0">
    How finished session branches reach the repository. Existing sessions keep
    their ship mode; changes apply to new sessions.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectShip"}}">
    {{template "csrf" $}}
    <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
    <div class="choice-row">
      <label class="choice">
        <input type="radio" name="directToPrimary" value="0" {{if not .ProjectItem.DirectToPrimary}}checked{{end}}>
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="t">Pull requests <span class="flag ok">default</span></span>
        <span class="d">Each session works a managed branch and opens a PR for review via <span class="mono">gh</span>.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="choice">
        <input type="radio" name="directToPrimary" value="1" {{if .ProjectItem.DirectToPrimary}}checked{{end}}>
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="t">Direct to primary <span class="flag warn">no review</span></span>
        <span class="d">Grok fast-forwards the <strong>Primary branch</strong> below (or origin default when empty) and pushes — no PR. Solo / fast-moving trusted projects only.</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="form-actions"><button type="submit">Save shipping</button></div>
  </form>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:1.1rem; padding-top:1rem;">
    <form class="inline" method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectPrimaryBranch"}}" id="project-primary-branch" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 22rem) auto;">
      {{template "csrf" $}}
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
      <div>
        <label for="project-primary-branch-input">Primary branch</label>
        <input type="text" id="project-primary-branch-input" name="primaryBranch" value="{{.ProjectItem.PrimaryBranch}}"
               maxlength="128" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9._-]+"
               placeholder="origin/HEAD heuristic (empty)" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
        {{if .ProjectItem.PrimaryBranchInvalid}}
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0; color:var(--danger, #b00); font-size:0.8rem">
          Stored value is invalid and is ignored until fixed.
        </p>
        {{end}}
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Save primary branch</button>
    </form>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
      Grokwork&rsquo;s default line for this project: new worktree base, direct-to-primary ship target,
      <span class="mono">/sync</span> merge base, commits browser default, deploy &ldquo;primary only&rdquo; allowlist,
      and Actions tip. It may <strong>differ</strong> from GitHub&rsquo;s repository default branch.
      Leave empty to follow <span class="mono">origin/HEAD</span> and common names (<span class="mono">main</span>,
      <span class="mono">master</span>, <span class="mono">prod</span>, &hellip;). Single branch name only
      (no <span class="mono">/</span>, no <span class="mono">origin/</span> prefix).
    </p>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
      <strong>Interim without this field:</strong> on the host checkout,
      <span class="mono">git remote set-head origin &lt;branch&gt;</span> retargets every heuristic that starts at
      <span class="mono">origin/HEAD</span> (local only; does not change GitHub). Prefer this field for a durable,
      UI-visible control and for PR <span class="mono">--base</span> / direct-mode forbid wording.
    </p>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
      If any catalog repo lacks this branch name on origin, surfaces that open that checkout will error when primary is set.
      Sessions that already stamped a primary at ship keep that name for <span class="mono">/sync</span> until reset;
      new worktrees use the configured primary immediately.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:1.1rem; padding-top:1rem;">
    <form method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectCherryPickTargets"}}" id="project-cherry-pick-targets">
      {{template "csrf" $}}
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
      <div>
        <label for="project-cherry-pick-targets-input">Cherry-pick targets</label>
        <textarea id="project-cherry-pick-targets-input" name="cherryPickTargets" rows="4" class="mono"
                  placeholder="staging&#10;production" spellcheck="false">{{.ProjectItem.CherryPickTargetsText}}</textarea>
        {{if .ProjectItem.CherryPickTargetsInvalid}}
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0; color:var(--danger, #b00); font-size:0.8rem">
          One or more stored names are invalid and are ignored until fixed.
        </p>
        {{end}}
      </div>
      <div class="form-actions"><button type="submit">Save cherry-pick targets</button></div>
    </form>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
      Long-lived branches the commits UI may cherry-pick onto (one name per line). Empty turns the
      button off. The project <strong>primary</strong> is never a valid target even if listed &mdash;
      that line is Direct-to-primary / pull requests. Single branch names only (no
      <span class="mono">/</span>, no <span class="mono">origin/</span>). At most 8.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section card" id="project-agent-mcp">
  <h2>Grokwork MCP</h2>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:0">
    In-session grokwork tools (tickets, Linear, ClickUp, storage, error sources).
    The host kill switch <span class="mono">agentMCP: false</span> still disables every attach.
    Explain / tools-off never attach. Cursor never attaches.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectAgentMCP"}}">
    {{template "csrf" $}}
    <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
    <div class="choice-row">
      <label class="choice">
        <input type="radio" name="agentMCPAlways" value="0" {{if not .ProjectItem.AgentMCPAlways}}checked{{end}}>
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="t">Default <span class="flag ok">safe</span></span>
        <span class="d">Ship/fix attach for every agent. Claude investigate gets a read-only mint. Grok investigate stays off (<span class="mono">--deny MCPTool</span>) so a repo <span class="mono">.grok/config.toml</span> cannot run MCP on a read-only turn.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="choice">
        <input type="radio" name="agentMCPAlways" value="1" {{if .ProjectItem.AgentMCPAlways}}checked{{end}}>
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="t">Always attach <span class="flag warn">trusted</span></span>
        <span class="d">Grok investigate and plan also attach grokwork MCP (read-only). Also attaches every other MCP server in the operator&rsquo;s user config and the worktree. Internal teams with no external members only.</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="form-actions"><button type="submit">Save MCP attach</button></div>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="section card" id="project-sessions">
  <h2>Sessions</h2>
  <form class="inline" method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectMode"}}" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 22rem) auto;">
    {{template "csrf" $}}
    <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
    <div>
      <label for="project-default-mode">Default mode</label>
      <select id="project-default-mode" name="defaultMode">
        {{$curMode := .ProjectItem.DefaultMode}}
        <option value="" {{if eq $curMode ""}}selected{{end}}>fix — implement &amp; ship (default)</option>
        <option value="case" {{if eq $curMode "case"}}selected{{end}}>case — support lifecycle</option>
        <option value="investigate" {{if eq $curMode "investigate"}}selected{{end}}>investigate — read-only</option>
        <option value="explain" {{if eq $curMode "explain"}}selected{{end}}>explain</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <button type="submit">Save mode</button>
  </form>
  <p class="sub" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">
    Support projects usually want <span class="mono">case</span> so freeform
    messages stay on the case lifecycle. Eng projects keep the default (fix).
  </p>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:1.1rem; padding-top:1rem;">
    <form class="inline" method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectCaseKey"}}" id="project-case-key" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 22rem) auto;">
      {{template "csrf" $}}
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
      <div>
        <label for="project-case-key-input">Case id prefix</label>
        {{/* maxlength mirrors the server's cap: a longer prefix would be minted
             truncated, so the field must not let one be typed and then quietly
             disagree with the ids. */}}
        <input type="text" id="project-case-key-input" name="caseKey" value="{{.ProjectItem.CaseKey}}"
               maxlength="10" pattern="[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]{0,9}"
               placeholder="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}" autocapitalize="characters" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Save case id</button>
    </form>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
      New cases are numbered <span class="mono">PREFIX-1</span>, <span class="mono">PREFIX-2</span>, … Empty derives the
      prefix from the project name. Changing it only affects cases filed afterwards — ids already
      quoted in commits and in other cases keep resolving.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:1.1rem; padding-top:1rem;">
    <form method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectSLA"}}" id="project-sla">
      {{template "csrf" $}}
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
      <label>Case SLA targets — minutes, empty means no deadline</label>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Severity</th><th>First response</th><th>Resolution</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {{range .ProjectItem.SLA}}
            <tr>
              <td><span class="case-sev sev-{{.Severity}}">{{.Severity}}</span></td>
              <td><input type="number" min="0" step="5" inputmode="numeric" name="first_{{.Severity}}" value="{{.FirstResponse}}" placeholder="none" aria-label="{{.Severity}} first response minutes"></td>
              <td><input type="number" min="0" step="5" inputmode="numeric" name="resolution_{{.Severity}}" value="{{.Resolution}}" placeholder="none" aria-label="{{.Severity}} resolution minutes"></td>
            </tr>
            {{end}}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
        Breach is computed when a board is drawn, never stored, so changing a target
        re-judges every open case immediately. The resolution clock <strong>pauses</strong> while a
        case sits in <span class="mono">answered</span> — that wait is the customer&rsquo;s, not ours. Cases filed
        before SLAs existed carry no start time and never breach.
        {{if not .ProjectItem.SLAConfigured}}<br>No targets set: this project&rsquo;s cases have no SLA.{{end}}
      </p>
      <div class="form-actions"><button type="submit">Save SLA targets</button></div>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:1.1rem; padding-top:1rem;">
    <form method="post" action="{{route "config.setProjectVerify"}}" id="project-verify">
      {{template "csrf" $}}
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{.ProjectItem.Name}}">
      <label for="project-verify-cmds">Verify commands — run by <span class="mono">@Grok /verify</span> or from a session in the web UI</label>
      <textarea id="project-verify-cmds" name="verifyCommands" rows="5" placeholder="unit | go test ./...&#10;lint | make lint | 300000" spellcheck="false">{{.ProjectItem.VerifyCommandsText}}</textarea>
      <p class="sub" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0; font-size:0.8rem">
        <span class="mono">name | command | timeoutMs?</span> per line (also <span class="mono">name: command</span>) ·
        runs in the session worktree, no model call · <span class="mono">#</span> comments · empty save clears all.
      </p>
      <div class="form-actions">
        <button type="submit">Save verify commands</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-secondary"
          data-grok-stream
          data-url="{{route "config.generateProjectVerify"}}"
          data-title="Suggest verify commands"
          data-subtitle="Inspecting the project checkout"
          data-fill="#project-verify-cmds"
          data-result-key="text"
          data-auto-close="900"
          title="Inspect the project checkout with Grok and draft verify commands (not saved until you Save)">Suggest with Grok</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
{{end}}
